Due to the enormous  varieties  in  optical  media,  is  made  as
generic  as  possible.  This can result in confusion.  Blanks and
then formats a CD‐RW disc using the format command.  It is recom‐
mended to use this command unless your drive  reports  that  it’s
not  supported;  in  that case, resort to the default Note that a
CD‐RW disc can be reformatted without  being  blanked.   Blanking
switches  between  sequential and fixed packet writing by erasing
the disc.  This can also help to revive old discs.  Format a  CD‐
RW  or a DVD+RW to use MRW (Mount Rainier).  This format tries to
hide media flaws as much as possible by relocation.  The  command
